WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.457
Unit 2 is what each government cloud has,
from the guide's availability table,

2
00:00:05.457 --> 00:00:09.062
read on Microsoft Learn on
November eleventh, 2026.

3
00:00:09.062 --> 00:00:15.164
Learn's page on Defender for Endpoint for
U S Government customers says prevention,

4
00:00:15.164 --> 00:00:18.347
detection, investigation and remediation

5
00:00:18.347 --> 00:00:21.000
are available in G C C,
G C C High and D O D.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.948
Each cloud has its own portal: security
dot microsoft dot com for G C C, security

7
00:00:26.948 --> 00:00:32.245
dot microsoft dot U S for G C C High,
and security dot apps dot mil for D O D.

8
00:00:32.245 --> 00:00:35.962
Graph's incident and hunting
A P I's are available,

9
00:00:35.962 --> 00:00:38.750
with G C C on the worldwide Graph host.

10
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.725
Then the gap.

11
00:00:39.725 --> 00:00:44.731
Learn's page on Security Exposure Management
says it's available in Public Cloud

12
00:00:44.731 --> 00:00:46.749
only, not in U S Government clouds,

13
00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:49.887
so attack paths and the
exposure graph aren't there.

14
00:00:49.887 --> 00:00:53.961
And Learn doesn't say whether custom
detection rules through Graph,

15
00:00:53.961 --> 00:00:59.126
automatic attack disruption, or web content
filtering on Windows reach these clouds.

16
00:00:59.126 --> 00:01:02.837
The guide's rule: not yet
specified means Learn doesn't say,

17
00:01:02.837 --> 00:01:04.338
not that it's available.

18
00:01:04.338 --> 00:01:08.319
A feature your cloud doesn't offer
goes in the decision record and

19
00:01:08.319 --> 00:01:12.360
the closure register as not
applicable, never as a failed control.
